From 6881d3eccb7f3307e9dfbf0589b1fccbbdd55151 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Katalyst Contributors <noreply@katalyst.dev>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 13:24:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] editor: Fix panic when showing pending input in a read-only
 buffer (#64730)

# Objective

Fixes ZED-BTA, ZED-8MC, ZED-875 and ZED-80K. Fixes FR-489.

When you have a binding like `j k`, Zed shows the `j` underlined while
it waits for the next key. We figured out where that `j` went by
assuming it was always inserted. In a read-only buffer it isn't, so with
the cursor at the end of the file we ended up pointing one character
past the end and crashed.

## Solution

We now take anchors at each cursor before inserting and read the
positions back from them afterwards, so we only highlight text that
actually made it into the buffer. This also covers other cases where the
insert gets dropped, like a read-only file inside project search. Also
removed the editor's own read-only check there, since it's no longer
needed.

## Testing

- `test_jk_pending_input_at_end_of_read_only_buffer` covers this and
panics without the fix.
- To reproduce on `main`: bind `"j k": "editor::Cancel"` in the `Editor`
context, put the cursor at the end of a file, run *workspace: toggle
read only file*, and press `j`.

